Write a JQF property-based test to reproduce this bug.

Project root: /home/byoungwoo/preserve-testing/experiments/main/workspace/Math-44/source
Test file: src/test/java/org/apache/commons/math/ode/events/JQF_EventStateTest.java
Test class: org.apache.commons.math.ode.events.JQF_EventStateTest
Test method: testBugReproduction

Bug summary: In Apache Commons Math ODE integrators (AbstractIntegrator.integrate/acceptStep event handling), when two events occur in the same step and the first one triggers a state reset, the integrator state/event handlers are not fully reinitialized. The second event then can't be located or handled correctly.

Concrete examples:
[{'input': 'Integrate an ODE with two EventHandlers whose events occur within the same step; the first handler returns RESET_STATE (or RESET_DERIVATIVES) when triggered.', 'expected': 'After the first event resets the state, the integrator fully reinitializes (including derivatives/interpolator and remaining event states) so that the second event in the same step is still found and handled at the right time.', 'actual': 'Reinitialization after the first event is incomplete, so the second event handler fails to find its event (it is missed or mislocated) in the remainder of the step.'}]

Use exactly this structure for the property-based test:
```java
package org.apache.commons.math.ode.events;

import static org.junit.Assert.*;
import static org.junit.Assume.assumeTrue;

import com.pholser.junit.quickcheck.*;
import com.pholser.junit.quickcheck.generator.*;
import edu.berkeley.cs.jqf.fuzz.*;
import org.junit.runner.RunWith;
import anonymous.log.Log;
// ... imports of the classes under test

@RunWith(JQF.class)
public class JQF_EventStateTest {

    @Fuzz
    public void testBugReproduction(@InRange(minInt = -100, maxInt = 100) int x,
